meta:
  origin:
    producer: Food and Agriculture Organization of the United Nations
    title: The State of World Fisheries and Aquaculture 2024
    description: |-
      The State of World Fisheries and Aquaculture (SOFIA) is FAO's flagship publication on the
      status, trends and outlook of world fisheries and aquaculture.

      This data covers the report's estimates of employment in the primary sector of fisheries and
      aquaculture: the number of people engaged as full-time, part-time, occasional or unspecified
      workers. Figures are given by geographical region and by subsector: aquaculture, inland
      fisheries, marine fisheries, and an "unspecified" category for workers who could not be
      assigned to a subsector. The data span the period 1995 to 2022; values for the 2000s and 2010s
      are reported as decade averages, while 1995, 2020 and 2022 are single years. Employment
      estimates for 1995-2021 were revised upward relative to earlier editions of the report. The
      underlying figures are compiled by FAO from national statistics and published in the FAO
      Yearbook of Fishery and Aquaculture Statistics.
    citation_full: 'FAO (2024). The State of World Fisheries and Aquaculture 2024. Blue Transformation in action. Rome. https://doi.org/10.4060/cd0683en'
    attribution_short: FAO
    url_main: https://openknowledge.fao.org/handle/20.500.14283/cd0683en
    date_accessed: '2026-07-08'
    date_published: '2024-06-07'
